From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v8-embed-feedstock <noreply@github.com>
Date: Mon, 1 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Hide abseil's symbols in a shared V8

v8.gyp builds every V8 target with -fvisibility=hidden, set once in its
target_defaults, so a shared build of V8 exports its own API and not the
libraries vendored underneath it.  abseil.gyp is a separate .gyp file and
inherits none of that, which leaves abseil the one part of the library
compiled at default visibility.

Measured on libv8.so.14.6.202.34 before this change: 973 exported absl::
symbols plus the AbslInternal* C entry points, against 0 for highway and
simdutf, which are targets inside v8.gyp.  V8's bundled zlib is unaffected
either way because Chromium's chromeconf.h renames it to Cr_z_*.

That matters for an embedder rather than for node.  A process that already
has an abseil -- conda's libprotobuf pulls one in, and it is built for a
different C++ standard than V8 uses -- ends up with two implementations
under identical mangled names, and the dynamic linker binds calls to
whichever object was loaded first.  The failure is a crash or quiet
misbehaviour at run time, not a link error.

Applies the same conditions v8.gyp's target_defaults uses, verbatim.  After
it, the library exports v8::, cppgc::, v8_inspector:: and weak std::
template instantiations, and nothing else.
---
 tools/v8_gypfiles/abseil.gyp | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/v8_gypfiles/abseil.gyp b/tools/v8_gypfiles/abseil.gyp
--- a/tools/v8_gypfiles/abseil.gyp
+++ b/tools/v8_gypfiles/abseil.gyp
@@ -377,6 +377,22 @@
             '<(ABSEIL_ROOT)/absl/time/internal/cctz/src/time_zone_name_win.cc',
           ],
         }],
+        # Same as v8.gyp's target_defaults.  This file is a separate .gyp and
+        # so does not inherit them, which leaves abseil the one part of a
+        # shared build of V8 compiled at default visibility: every absl::
+        # symbol lands in the library's dynamic symbol table, where it can be
+        # interposed with a different abseil in the same process.
+        ['OS=="mac"', {
+          'xcode_settings': {
+            'GCC_SYMBOLS_PRIVATE_EXTERN': 'YES',  # -fvisibility=hidden
+            'GCC_INLINES_ARE_PRIVATE_EXTERN': 'YES',  # -fvisibility-inlines-hidden
+          },
+        }, '(OS!="aix" and OS!="os400") and (OS!="win" or clang==1)', {
+          'cflags': [
+            '-fvisibility=hidden',
+            '-fvisibility-inlines-hidden',
+          ],
+        }],
       ],
     },  # abseil
   ]
